---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Base
  title="Terms — Nakvali"
  description="Terms for using the early-stage Nakvali cycling recorder and website."
>
  <article class="document">
    <p class="eyebrow">BEFORE YOU RIDE</p>
    <h1>Terms of use.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Nakvali is an independent, early-stage cycling recorder. Use it
      thoughtfully and keep a backup of the rides that matter to you.
    </p>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: {site.updated}</p>
    <h2>The app and website</h2>
    <p>
      Nakvali is developed by Stas (
      <a href="https://github.com/whekin">whekin</a>). These terms apply to the
      app and this website. Using Nakvali means accepting these terms. If you do
      not agree, stop using the service. Any rights granted by an explicit
      source-code or dependency license remain governed by that license.
    </p>
    <h2>Early development</h2>
    <p>
      The app is under active development. Features may change, and recording,
      sensor estimates, exports or connected services may fail or be
      unavailable. Keep independent backups of important rides. Features marked
      “coming soon” are plans, not a promise of delivery or a feature of the
      current build.
    </p>
    <h2>Ride responsibly</h2>
    <p>
      Nakvali is not an emergency, navigation or safety service. Recorded tracks
      and statistics are estimates, not guarantees of trail access, safety or
      timing accuracy. Follow local rules and trail closures, respect other
      riders and landowners, and stop somewhere safe before interacting with
      your phone.
    </p>
    <h2>Your recordings and account</h2>
    <p>
      You keep your rights in your recordings. Using the app does not transfer
      ownership of them to Nakvali. You authorize the processing necessary for
      the features you use, such as local track processing or an export you
      request. Keep your account credentials secure and upload only recordings
      you are entitled to share.
    </p>
    <h2>Other services</h2>
    <p>
      Google/Firebase, GitHub, map providers and any ride-sharing service you
      choose have their own terms and privacy practices. Nakvali is an
      independent project and is not made by or endorsed by BIKEYARD.
      Connecting to a service does not guarantee that it will accept a ride or
      calculate the same statistics.
    </p>
    <h2>Availability and responsibility</h2>
    <p>
      To the extent permitted by applicable law, Nakvali is provided as
      available without a guarantee of uninterrupted operation or error-free
      results. Nothing in these terms excludes rights or responsibilities that
      cannot legally be excluded. You can stop using the app at any time;
      deleting the app does not automatically delete data previously sent to
      other services.
    </p>
    <h2>Privacy and contact</h2>
    <p>
      Read the <a href="/privacy">Privacy notice</a> for details about data
      handling and deletion requests.
    </p>
    {site.contactEmail ? (
      <p>
        Questions about these terms:{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    ) : (
      <p class="notice">
        Preview: a contact address must be configured before these terms are
        published.
      </p>
    )}
  </article>
</Base>
